// @title   TropeLang Concept Library — Dynamics
// @version 1.0
// @note    Process and dynamic concepts — the motions of motivation, conflict,
//          persuasion, social power, and narrative structure. Unlike static
//          conditions, these name things that unfold, escalate, or resolve over
//          time. They appear as edge targets across tropes and modules:
//          a scheme runs on misdirection, a rivalry on attrition, a payoff on
//          earlier investment.
//
// Import: import "trl/concepts/dynamics.trl"


// =============================================================================
// MOTIVATION AND WILL
// =============================================================================

// The drive toward attainment beyond one's present station; the reach for more.
// Ambition is directional and open-ended — it names the wanting, not the having.
concept ambition         [+Abstract]

// Firm belief held as settled truth; the steadiness from which one acts.
// Conviction precedes and outlasts evidence; it is what doubt erodes.
concept conviction       [+Abstract]

// The binding of oneself to a course, person, or cause beyond easy retreat.
// Commitment converts intention into obligation — it raises the cost of turning back.
concept commitment       [+Abstract]

// The hardened will to see a thing through despite cost or resistance.
// Resolve is conviction under pressure — tested, not merely held.
concept resolve          [+Abstract]

// The fixation of will on a single object until it crowds out all else.
// Obsession is desire that has lost proportion; it consumes the one who carries it.
concept obsession        [+Abstract]

// The sense that an outcome is appointed and will arrive regardless of resistance.
// Destiny names a future that pulls rather than a present that pushes.
concept destiny          [+Abstract] [+Inevitable]

// The use of a thing, person, or act as a means toward some further end.
// The instrumental is never wanted for itself — its value is borrowed from its purpose.
concept instrumental     [+Abstract]

// The condition of a need or drive overriding all competing concerns.
// Prepotency names the urge that takes precedence — what must be answered first.
concept prepotency       [+Abstract]

// The ripening of a self over time into fuller capacity or understanding.
// Maturation is becoming made gradual — growth measured against who one was.
concept maturation       [+Abstract]

// The draining of will or hope; the sapping of the drive to continue.
// Discouragement is not yet defeat — it is the weakening that precedes it.
concept discouragement   [+Abstract] [#Painful]

// The settling into acceptance of an unwanted condition one has ceased to fight.
// Resignation differs from acceptance: it yields without peace.
concept resignation      [+Abstract]


// =============================================================================
// EMOTION
// =============================================================================

// The thwarting of a drive that has no outlet; will met by a wall.
// Frustration is desire blocked, accumulating pressure with nowhere to go.
concept frustration      [+Abstract] [#Painful]

// The completion of a longing or purpose; a need brought to its rest.
// Fulfillment names the arrival, not the journey — wanting answered.
concept fulfillment      [+Abstract]

// The settled pleasure of having enough; a desire met without excess.
// Satisfaction is quieter than joy and more durable than relief.
concept satisfaction     [+Abstract]

// The easing that follows the lifting of a threat, pain, or strain.
// Relief is defined by what precedes it — it cannot exist without prior tension.
concept relief           [+Abstract]

// The light pleasure of the incongruous or playful; delight without stakes.
// Amusement is brief and surface-level — it asks nothing and leaves no mark.
concept amusement        [+Abstract]

// The pull toward the unknown; the appetite to know what is hidden or withheld.
// Curiosity is desire pointed at information — it is what mysteries exploit.
concept curiosity        [+Abstract]

// The jolt of the unexpected; expectation overturned in an instant.
// Surprise is the gap between what was anticipated and what arrived.
concept surprise         [+Abstract]

// Feeling that moves the witness to pity or sorrow; suffering made affecting.
// Pathos is the quality by which another's pain reaches and claims us.
concept pathos           [+Abstract] [#Painful]


// =============================================================================
// COGNITION AND PERSUASION
// =============================================================================

// The construction of acceptable reasons for what was done from other motives.
// Rationalization makes the chosen look justified after the fact.
concept rationalization  [+Abstract]

// The margin of uncertainty sufficient to withhold judgment or conviction.
// Reasonable doubt is the gap a case must close — the room left for innocence.
concept reasonable_doubt [+Abstract]

// The pushing of an unwanted truth or feeling below conscious reach.
// Repression hides a thing from oneself; what is buried persists and presses.
concept repression       [+Abstract]

// The deliberate keeping of a truth from those who would act on it.
// Concealment hides from others what they would otherwise see.
concept concealment      [+Abstract]

// The steering of attention away from what matters toward what does not.
// Misdirection wins not by hiding the truth but by aiming the eye elsewhere.
concept misdirection     [+Abstract]

// The clearing of a name or position by proof against prior doubt or accusation.
// Vindication is conviction confirmed by outcome — being shown to have been right.
concept vindication      [+Abstract]

// The recoil of a scheme upon the one who set it; harm returned to its source.
// Backfire names the plan that becomes the agent's own undoing.
concept backfire         [+Abstract] [+Paradoxical]

// The shift of a belief or allegiance from one side toward its opposite.
// Swing is persuasion in motion — the moment a held position gives way.
concept swing            [+Abstract]


// =============================================================================
// SOCIAL AND POWER
// =============================================================================

// The joining of separate parties into a common front for shared ends.
// A coalition is unity assembled, not given — it holds only while interests align.
concept coalition        [%Political] [+Abstract] [+Fragile]

// The recognized right to hold power or be obeyed; authority others accept.
// Legitimacy is granted, not seized — it lives in the consent of those it governs.
concept legitimacy       [%Political] [+Abstract] [+Fragile]

// The seizing of a position or right that belongs to another.
// Usurpation takes power without legitimacy — the throne held against its claim.
concept usurpation       [%Political] [+Abstract]

// The discouraging of an act by raising its expected cost beyond its gain.
// Deterrence works by threat held in reserve — it succeeds when nothing happens.
concept deterrence       [%Political] [+Abstract]

// The aligning of separate actors toward a joint result they could not reach alone.
// Coordination is the structure beneath cooperation — who moves when, and with whom.
concept coordination     [+Abstract]

// The settlement reached when each party yields part of its claim.
// Compromise resolves by mutual loss — neither side prevails, both consent.
concept compromise       [+Abstract]

// The use of another's labor, need, or weakness for one's own gain.
// Exploitation extracts value from a relation of unequal power.
concept exploitation     [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract]

// The shielding of the vulnerable from harm by one who stands between.
// Protection is care made active — the guarding of what cannot guard itself.
concept protection       [+Abstract]

// The fitting-together of parts into a balanced, self-sustaining whole.
// Harmony is order that feels effortless — concord without strain.
concept harmony          [+Abstract] [+Fragile]

// The setting of one thing against another so each defines the other by difference.
// Contrast generates meaning through opposition — the light known by the dark.
concept contrast         [+Abstract]


// =============================================================================
// CONFLICT AND TACTICS
// =============================================================================

// The forceful pressing toward another with intent to harm, dominate, or seize.
// Aggression is conflict initiated — the first move that forces a response.
concept aggression       [+Abstract]

// The warding-off of attack; the holding of ground against a pressing force.
// Defense answers aggression — it succeeds by denying, not by gaining.
concept defense          [+Abstract]

// The grinding-down of an opponent through sustained, cumulative cost.
// Attrition wins not by a blow but by outlasting — the slow exhaustion of the other.
concept attrition        [+Abstract]

// The forcing of a boundary, defense, or barrier that was meant to hold.
// A breach is the point where what enclosed gives way.
concept breach           [+Abstract]

// A sudden outward strike from a defended position against those besieging it.
// A sortie trades the safety of the wall for the initiative of the sally.
concept sortie           [+Abstract]

// The locked stalemate where neither side can advance nor afford to yield.
// Deadlock is conflict frozen — force met by equal force, motion canceled.
concept deadlock         [+Abstract]

// The unwelcome entry into a space, body, or order that was closed against it.
// Intrusion violates a boundary — presence where presence was not permitted.
concept intrusion        [+Abstract]

// An intricate scheme executed by a skilled team against a hard target.
// A caper is conflict as choreography — its pleasure is in the precision of the plan.
concept caper            [+Abstract]

// The sudden failure of a structure, order, or will that had been holding.
// Collapse is the moment accumulated strain exceeds what can bear it.
concept collapse         [+Abstract]


// =============================================================================
// NARRATIVE AND STRUCTURE
// =============================================================================

// The deferred return on something earlier set up; the cashing-in of a setup.
// A payoff redeems a prior promise — it depends on what was planted before it.
concept payoff           [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The holding of attention; the grip a story keeps on those it has drawn in.
// Engagement is the live tension between audience and unfolding — interest sustained.
concept engagement       [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// What stands to be won or lost; the weight that makes an outcome matter.
// Stakes name the cost of failure — without them, events carry no tension.
concept stakes           [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The turning of a situation to its opposite; fortune swung from up to down or back.
// Reversal is the hinge of a plot — the moment direction flips.
concept reversal         [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The turning of a pattern inside-out so its terms exchange roles.
// Inversion preserves the structure while reversing what fills it.
concept inversion        [%Narrative] [+Abstract] [+Paradoxical]

// The earlier commitment of resources or attention that a later payoff draws upon.
// Investment is what is risked or planted now in expectation of a return later.
concept investment       [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The rendering of events into a told sequence; the giving of shape to what happened.
// An account is experience narrated — selected, ordered, and addressed to a listener.
concept account          [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The making of a way forward from whatever is at hand, without a prior plan.
// Improvisation is order composed in the moment — design under time's pressure.
concept improvisation    [+Abstract]

// A three-sided relation whose tensions arise from the impossibility of all three holding.
// The triangle is structure as predicament — three pulls that cannot all be satisfied.
concept triangle         [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract] [+Fragile]

// A bond whose ending is written into its beginning; love bent toward loss.
// Doomed love draws its force from the certainty of its ruin.
concept doomed_love      [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract] [+Inevitable]

// The return of a broken order to wholeness; a prior positive state regained.
// Restoration undoes a fall — it carries the memory of what was lost in the having-back.
concept restoration      [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The dynamic by which a belief, once held, brings about the very thing it expected.
// The self-fulfilling outcome is caused by the prediction of it — expectation made real.
concept self_fulfilling  [+Abstract] [+Paradoxical]


// =============================================================================
// NAMED PATTERNS — base concepts that the trope registry also tag-mutates
// =============================================================================
// These name a dynamic in its own right AND have a formalized trope. The base
// concept lives here; trl/tropes/index.trl applies [+Trope] provenance to it
// (a tag-mutation, not a redeclaration — the registry's DRY convention). Edges
// across modules and tropes reference the bare concept, founded via this library.

// The decisive ending blow that converts an advantage into a settled defeat.
// A finishing move closes a contest — it is the strike that makes the win final.
concept finishing_move   [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract]

// A defense held to the end against hopeless odds, ground bought with everything left.
// The last stand wins time or meaning, not survival — it succeeds by not yielding.
concept last_stand       [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract]

// The turning of an attacker's own committed force back against them.
// A counter answers aggression by using its momentum — defense that becomes the blow.
concept counter          [%Interpersonal] [+Abstract]

// The breaking of a united adversary into parts too weak to resist apart.
// Divide and conquer defeats coordination — it wins the pieces it could not win whole.
concept divide_and_conquer  [%Political] [+Abstract]

// The summons that opens a journey; the disturbance that asks the ordinary to leave it.
// A call to adventure names the threshold offered — the world's invitation to change.
concept call_to_adventure   [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The hesitation or rejection that meets the summons; the pull of the world left behind.
// Refusal of the call is the journey deferred — fear, duty, or comfort holding the line.
concept refusal_of_the_call [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The withholding of resolution at a height of tension, suspending the outcome.
// A cliffhanger spends suspense as a hook — it ends by refusing to end.
concept cliffhanger      [%Narrative] [+Abstract]

// The guilt of the spared toward those who were not; survival felt as debt.
// Survivor's guilt turns deliverance into burden — to have lived where others did not.
concept survivors_guilt  [%Psychological] [+Abstract]

// The earlier planting of what a later payoff redeems; the promise a story makes to itself.
// A setup is meaning deferred — significance placed now to be collected later.
concept setup            [%Narrative] [+Abstract]
